WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 5.4 · Internal Systems & Operations
The planning and reporting calendar

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Put all your yearly cycles on one calendar from your first year to avoid last-minute rushes.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:25.911
A planning and reporting calendar puts all your yearly cycles in one place: strategy review, annual plan and budget, quarterly reviews, monthly finance, meetings, reports, legal filings and policy reviews.

4
00:00:26.311 --> 00:00:26.911
Three layers on one calendar

5
00:00:26.911 --> 00:00:38.981
Fixed dates: Financial year end, legal deadlines, founders' or board meetings and reports you already owe. For example: The bakery's deadline for filing accounts and its yearly meeting with the advisory group.

6
00:00:38.981 --> 00:00:50.311
Internal reviews: Plan, budget and reviews placed early enough to inform the fixed dates. For example: The bakery drafts its plan in September, so the budget is ready for November.

7
00:00:50.311 --> 00:01:03.952
Your own seasons: School terms, harvests, festivals, rainy seasons, busy months and months when cash is tight. For example: The bakery marks December as its busiest month and February as its tightest for cash.

8
00:01:04.352 --> 00:01:04.952
Why one calendar

9
00:01:04.952 --> 00:01:08.774
1. It prevents clashes and last-minute rushes.

10
00:01:08.774 --> 00:01:15.189
2. The budget follows the plan and arrives before the meeting that approves it.

11
00:01:15.189 --> 00:01:21.122
3. You see tight months coming and prepare for them.

12
00:01:21.522 --> 00:01:22.122
What it connects

13
00:01:22.122 --> 00:01:27.426
1. Your strategy from Module 1 gives the calendar its objectives.

14
00:01:27.426 --> 00:01:32.359
2. Your governance calendar and reporting rhythm from Module 3.

15
00:01:32.359 --> 00:01:38.663
3. Your weekly and quarterly routines, which bring it to life.

16
00:01:39.063 --> 00:01:39.663
What to avoid

17
00:01:39.663 --> 00:01:43.485
Planning forwards and missing fixed deadlines.

18
00:01:43.485 --> 00:01:48.048
Leaving out your own seasons and cash-tight months.

19
00:01:48.048 --> 00:01:54.722
Dropping unknown dates instead of marking them “to confirm when registered”.

20
00:01:55.322 --> 00:01:57.122
You draft your first annual planning and reporting calendar.

21
00:01:57.122 --> 00:02:01.122
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

22
00:02:02.622 --> 00:02:05.722
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
